      "instance_name": "school_setting",
      "label": "school setting",
      "description": "The image depicts a child in a lab coat and safety goggles holding a bomb in front of a chalkboard, which is a common visual trope for a classroom or school environment. Understanding that this is a school setting is essential to interpret the meme's context — the 'teacher roasting' and the 'bomb going off' are framed as occurring in a school context, which adds to the humor and absurdity of the situation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_03b1e002"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2a0a9890",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "teacher_roasting",
      "label": "teacher roasting",
      "description": "The phrase 'teacher roasts you' refers to a common social phenomenon in schools where a teacher publicly criticizes or makes fun of a student, often in a humorous or sarcastic way. This is a cultural reference to classroom dynamics and is not directly visible in the image but is essential to understand the meme's premise.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
